From 93ae752cdd3d2ad3a9c88260dc42b31164fbd6da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 06:17:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Ingestion: traceable rejections, undated-record flag,
 explicit forwards keep their origin root (under review)

D1 holder migration 0004 ingest_rejections: every refused input item gets a content-free
disposition row (locator, raw hash, stage, reason) written with the cursor advance; SyncReport and
connector health report it (degraded/rejected_items). D2 records without a usable timestamp are
ingested with time_inferred and take the source's content time, never presenting as fresh.
D3 an explicit forward/share link gives the record the origin's object identity and root, so the
original and forwards-with-commentary in other holders count as one independent root.
Engineer: ENGINEER-D (claude-sonnet-5-5). Full suite on the shared tree: 434 passed, 7 skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QgQYqiZ8KjrbuXgxGadraA
